{"id": 25, "ts": 1779492339.699113, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "I\u2019d like to bring two points forward. First, from my interview notes Candidate\u202fC is described as\u202f100\u202f% reliable and consistently creates a positive atmosphere with his crew \u2013 a rare combination of operational reliability and crew\u2011cooperation that we have not seen confirmed for any other candidate. Second, while Candidate\u202fC does have communication\u2011style concerns (difficulty articulating ideas, perceived egocentricity) and a low willingness for further education, these are areas that can be addressed through targeted coaching and development plans. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB\u2019s reliability rests only on a conscientiousness proxy and his documented grumpiness and uncooperativeness raise higher crew\u2011interaction risk, and Candidate\u202fA and D lack any concrete reliability evidence and show notable leadership or attitude deficits. Therefore, I propose we provisionally prioritize Candidate\u202fC, while we still seek concrete reliability data (flight\u2011log consistency, incident history, punctuality) for all four candidates to validate the 100\u202f% claim and ensure no hidden safety concerns.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_1\", \"vote\": \"Candidate C\"}"}
