{"id": 35, "ts": 1779492397.8645713, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "**Public Message:**\nWe now have confirmation that none of us possess concrete operational\u2011reliability data (flight logs, incident history, punctuality) for any candidate, including Candidate\u202fC\u2019s 100\u202f% reliability claim. This leaves reliability as an **unverified** criterion for all four.\nGiven this gap, the next decisive comparison should focus on **crew\u2011cooperation and professional communication**, where we have the most concrete observations:\n- **Candidate\u202fB** \u2013 documented grumpy, uncooperative, pretentious, and occasional inappropriate tone.\n- **Candidate\u202fC** \u2013 difficulty articulating ideas and perceived egocentricity, but consistently creates a positive crew atmosphere and shows genuine concern for others.\n- **Candidate\u202fA** \u2013 unfriendly, shows\u2011off attitude, and unhealthy habits that may affect teamwork.\n- **Candidate\u202fD** \u2013 moody, loner, with a hot temper that could impair crew dynamics.\nTo move toward a recommendation, we should weigh which of these crew\u2011cooperation profiles is most manageable with coaching, given the lack of hard reliability evidence for all. I suggest we discuss whether Candidate\u202fC\u2019s positive crew atmosphere outweighs his communication style issues compared with Candidate\u202fB\u2019s more severe uncooperative behavior.\n**Vote:** Candidate C\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_3\", \"vote\": \"Candidate C\"}"}
